WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — time-as-an-index (45s) Narrator Hakim

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.146
First, inside a mathematical time loop,

2
00:00:03.146 --> 00:00:08.658
almost every digital lock would break at once except a one-time secret pad.

3
00:00:09.098 --> 00:00:13.476
Second, in known physics, no quantum trick, analog circuit,

4
00:00:13.476 --> 00:00:17.927
or reported anomaly sends readable answers backward in time.

5
00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:23.189
Third, every fast lookup of a future answer is work paid upfront,

6
00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.528
which fresh random values defeat immediately.

7
00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:33.232
You can print a giant answer book for fixed puzzles only by solving every single puzzle ahead of time.

8
00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:39.188
Roll fresh dice right before asking the question, and that entire pre-printed book stops working.

9
00:00:39.628 --> 00:00:45.332
Thirty-one machine-checked mathematical proofs confirm that without physical time loops,

10
00:00:45.332 --> 00:00:52.268
fresh random challenges and information-theoretic one-time secret pads keep future states safely unindexed.
